---
// terms.astro — Archex Ecosystem Terms of Service
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Archex"
  description="Terms governing the use of the Archex parent brand gateway (archexweb.in) and practice relationships."
  canonical="https://www.archexweb.in/terms/"
  activePath="/terms"
>
  <div class="shell legal-container">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <span class="tech-tag">Legal & Operating Terms</span>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Terms of Service<span class="hl-dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">
        <span>Effective Date: November 2026</span>
        <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
        <span>Applies to: archexweb.in</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Indian Legal Review Advisory Callout -->
    <div class="legal-advisory" role="note">
      <div class="advisory-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
          <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
          <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="advisory-text">
        <strong>Legal Notice & Indian Regulatory Context:</strong>
        These Website Terms govern access to and use of this informational parent gateway. Commercial agreements, statements of work, and professional deliverables are entered into separately and remain subject to specific written contracts governed under the laws of India.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Operating Identity & Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Archex</strong> is an independently operated brand managed by <strong>Kaif</strong>, an individual based in West Bengal, India.
        </p>
        <p>
          Archex is not a separately incorporated company or limited liability partnership. References to "Archex", "we", "us" and "our" refer to the individual operating the brand, unless the context indicates otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
          By accessing or navigating the website at <strong>archexweb.in</strong> (the "Website"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service and all applicable laws and regulations. If you do not agree with any of these terms, your sole remedy is to cease using the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Ecosystem Structure & Nature of Engagements</h2>
        <p>
          Archex functions as the parent brand and central information gateway for three complementary disciplines:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Archex Craft:</strong> Software engineering, digital product development, and technical systems (craft.archexweb.in). Also serves as the central contact and enquiry intake destination.</li>
          <li><strong>Archex Studio:</strong> Brand identity, creative direction, UI/UX, and digital experiences (studio.archexweb.in).</li>
          <li><strong>Archex GTM:</strong> Go-to-market strategy, positioning, and growth execution (gtm.archexweb.in; under development).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All three practices operate under the same individual founder and are not independent incorporated businesses.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Informational Gateway Only:</strong> This Website serves an informational and routing purpose. Submitting an enquiry or initial message through our central contact portal does not constitute or create a binding commercial contract, partnership, or retainer. Any professional engagement, technical deliverable, design work, or advisory service is executed strictly through a separate written proposal, Statement of Work (SOW), or Master Services Agreement (MSA) accepted by both parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
        <p>
          The content, layout, design, graphics, wordmarks, code, and documentation on archexweb.in are the exclusive property of Archex, protected under Indian and international copyright and intellectual property laws.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may view, print, or download informational materials from this Website solely for personal, non-commercial evaluation of our practices. You must not republish, reproduce, duplicate, modify, or commercially exploit any material from this Website without prior written permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Permissible Use & External Routing</h2>
        <p>
          This parent website is provided for informational and brand navigation purposes. When accessing this Website or using its routing links, you agree to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access the Website solely through lawful methods and standard web navigation interfaces.</li>
          <li>Refrain from transmitting unsolicited automated requests, denial-of-service attempts, malicious code, or scraping scripts.</li>
          <li>Not probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of the Website or attempt to bypass edge security or content delivery mechanisms.</li>
          <li>When following links to submit enquiries via Archex Craft (<a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/contact">craft.archexweb.in/contact</a>), provide genuine, accurate information and comply with the specific terms governing that destination.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. No Misleading Guarantees & Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The materials on this Website are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. Archex makes no warranties, expressed or implied, regarding commercial outcomes, revenue projections, search engine rankings, or uninterrupted availability.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not make exaggerated claims, provide fabricated credentials, or guarantee uniform results across client projects. Every engagement is evaluated on its specific technical, creative, and commercial merits.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, in no event shall Archex or its operator be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages (including loss of data, profit, goodwill, or business interruption) arising out of the use or inability to use this Website, even if advised of the possibility of such damage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Governing Law & Jurisdiction</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India, without regard to conflict of law principles. Any legal disputes arising out of the use of this Website shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts in West Bengal, India.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>8. Contact & Communications</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding these Terms or wish to communicate regarding website policies, please reach out via email at <a href="mailto:hello@archexweb.in">hello@archexweb.in</a> or through our centralised portal at <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/contact">craft.archexweb.in/contact</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-container {
    padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(60px, 9vw, 110px);
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .hl-dot {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .meta-sep {
    color: var(--line);
  }

  /* Advisory Callout */
  .legal-advisory {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--signal);
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .advisory-icon {
    color: var(--signal);
    margin-top: 2px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .advisory-text {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
  }

  .legal-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 20px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-section li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--signal);
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--signal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>

